---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" description="Hritik Kumar — software engineer making complex tech simple: system design and AI agents for developers, practical AI for everyone.">
  <div class="container about-wrap">
    <header class="about-header">
      <div class="about-avatar" aria-hidden="true">HK</div>
      <div>
        <h1>Hi, I'm Hritik.</h1>
        <p class="kicker">Software Developer · Oracle</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="about-body">
      <p>
        I'm a software developer at Oracle with around four years of experience building
        both small and large-scale applications. Most of my day-to-day involves
        stream-processing pipelines and the databases underneath them — and my mission
        here is simple: <strong>make complex tech simple</strong>.
      </p>
      <p>
        ByteScribble runs on two tracks. For developers, I write and film deep-dives on
        system design, software craft, and AI agents — the explanation I wish I'd had
        when I first met each topic, written down while the confusion is still fresh
        enough to remember. For everyone else, I make <a href="/topics/everyday-ai/">Everyday
        AI</a> content: practical, jargon-free ways to actually use AI in daily life.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also building <strong>Manaska</strong>, an adaptive learning platform, and
        documenting the real decisions behind it in
        <a href="/topics/build-in-public/">Build in Public</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Long-form deep-dives live on the <a href="/blog/">blog</a>, shorter thoughts land in
        <a href="/scribbles/">Scribbles</a>, and the <a href="/playground/">playground</a> is
        where I put the little games I build to procrastinate on writing.
      </p>

      <div class="about-now panel">
        <p class="now-label mono">Currently</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Starting a YouTube channel — system design deep-dives and everyday AI, new video every two weeks</li>
          <li>Building Manaska, an adaptive learning platform (devlogs coming)</li>
          <li>Writing a series on stream processing internals — Flink, Kafka, and CDC</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="about-contact">
        Say hello: <a href="mailto:hritik@bytescribble.com">hritik@bytescribble.com</a> ·
        <a href="https://github.com/Hrtkk" rel="me">GitHub</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@_byte_scribble" rel="me">YouTube</a> ·
        <a href="https://www.instagram.com/ByteScribble" rel="me">Instagram</a>
      </p>
      <p class="about-footnote">Thank you for being part of this journey!</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-wrap { max-width: 760px; }
  .about-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: 64px 0 34px;
  }
  .about-header h1 { font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .about-avatar {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 84px;
    height: 84px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--acc-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--acc-line);
    color: var(--acc);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 26px;
  }
  .about-body { font-size: 17.5px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .about-body p { margin: 0 0 1.2em; }
  .about-now { padding: 22px 26px; margin: 30px 0; }
  .now-label {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: .09em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--acc);
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  .about-now ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.3em; }
  .about-now li { margin-bottom: .4em; }
  .about-contact { font-size: 16px; }
  .about-footnote { color: var(--fg-3); font-style: italic; font-family: var(--serif); }
</style>
